PROPOSED — r0 row MOVED, never re-cut in place.

`evidence/w7/loop/r0/r6-idiom-history/hue-census.mjs` ends by printing the golden-angle walk
from a HARDCODED literal (`hue = i * 137.5`), not from `playerIdentity.inkFor`. Under PAL-TIN
that walk does not exist: the census would keep printing eight hues no page can paint. The
instrument reads every other row out of `index.css`; the tail is the one row that reads a
memory. This re-cut makes the tail read the same file as the rest.

The instrument writes NOTHING (stdout only, no `OUT` path), so nothing needed re-pointing
before it was run — the r0 copy in this lane's dir is byte-identical to r0's and was run
read-only. The r0 row is reported MOVED because its SUBJECT (the player palette) moves.

--- a/evidence/w7/loop/r0/r6-idiom-history/hue-census.mjs
+++ b/evidence/w7/loop/pass2/research/PAL-TIN/instruments/hue-census.mjs
@@ -100,9 +100,26 @@
-// The golden-angle player walk, against the same circle.
-console.log("\nplayer walk (playerIdentity.inkFor, hue = i * 137.5 mod 360), first 8:");
-for (let i = 0; i < 8; i++)
-  console.log(`  player ${i}: h=${((i * 137.5) % 360).toFixed(1)} deg @ C 0.110`);
+// THE PLAYER PALETTE, READ RATHER THAN REMEMBERED. The tail used to print `i * 137.5` from a
+// literal, which said nothing about the tree it was run on: it printed the same eight hues
+// whether the walk shipped, was re-cut, or had been replaced by a table. The census's own
+// discipline is "read the stylesheet"; this row now obeys it.
+const peers = [];
+for (const [regime, block] of [["light", light], ["dark", dark]])
+  for (let i = 1; i <= 16; i++) {
+    const hex = read(block, `--color-peer-${i}`);
+    if (!hex) continue;
+    const { L, C, h } = hexToOklch(hex);
+    peers.push({ i, regime, hex, L: +L.toFixed(3), C: +C.toFixed(3), h: +h.toFixed(1) });
+  }
+if (peers.length) {
+  console.log(`\nplayer palette (--color-peer-N, read from index.css): ${peers.length / 2} sticks, two arms`);
+  for (const p of peers)
+    console.log(`  peer-${p.i} ${p.regime}: ${p.hex}  L=${p.L} C=${p.C} h=${p.h}`);
+} else {
+  // No table: the tree still carries the formula. Print what the MODULE emits, not a literal.
+  const src = fs.readFileSync(path.join(import.meta.dirname, "../../../../../../../../web/frontend/src/games/shared/playerIdentity.ts"), "utf8");
+  const step = /%\s*360|\*\s*([\d.]+)/.exec(src.slice(src.indexOf("export const inkFor")));
+  console.log(`\nplayer walk (playerIdentity.inkFor, step ${step?.[1] ?? "?"} deg), first 8:`);
+  for (let i = 0; i < 8; i++)
+    console.log(`  player ${i}: h=${((i * Number(step?.[1] ?? 0)) % 360).toFixed(1)} deg`);
+}

